   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Marcus. You're verified. I checked order O-5108 from Big Slice Pizza. It was promised by 6:00 PM and delivered at 7:20 PM, which is 80 minutes late. I'm sorry it spoiled the party.\n\nUnder our late-delivery policy, I've added **$15.00 in account credit** to your account. That's 20% of your $92.00 subtotal, which is $18.40, capped at $15. You can use it on a future order. Late deliveries get account credit rather than a refund to your card.\n\nIf you'd like to talk with a person, I can also pass your case to a specialist. They would follow up within 24 hours. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "That's not good enough. I wanted $40 back, and $15 in account credit doesn't even cover the wings. Another delivery app gave me $50 once when something like this happened, so I know you can do better than this."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand you're frustrated, Marcus, and I'm sorry. I can't go beyond the $15 credit. Our policy sets late-delivery compensation at 20% of the subtotal, capped at $15. It's credit only, and I can't give a refund to your card or a goodwill amount on top of it. What another company did doesn't change what I'm allowed to do here.\n\nYour options are:\n- **Keep the $15 credit.** It's already on your account.\n- **Speak to a person.** I can hand your case to a specialist who will follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'll decide.\n- **Report a separate problem.** If any items were missing or wrong, or if anyone had a food-safety problem, tell me. Those are handled under different rules.\n\nWould you like me to escalate this to a specialist?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Fine, but I'm not happy about it. The $15 is what you're offering, so I'll take it for now. Don't escalate anything on my behalf, I'm done with this. And for the record, I've had worse service from an app that actually cared about keeping customers."
  }
